  "notes": "The isolated letters (1:1) are not glossed. A book for «آيات الكتاب وقرآن مبين». 2: the tafsirs place the wish at different times (leaving the Fire / at death and in the Hereafter), so only As-Sa'di's neutral «وقد فات وقت الإمكان». «ذرهم» addresses the Prophet ﷺ: no plate on it; an hourglass for «فسوف يعلمون» and «ولها كتاب معلوم». 4 keeps «وما أهلكنا… إلا» whole. STAGING v4: 1: believers sitting in a prayer hall read the Book (As-Sa'di: it must be received with acceptance); a book plate on 1:3. 2-3: a group of deniers in a market at dusk sits down to eat and talk (3:2-5: eating, enjoying, diverted by hope); the wish of verse 2 is not acted out (the tafsirs place it at different moments, in the Hereafter or at death); hourglass on 3:6. 4-5: the people of a town walk off the stage on 5:5 (their term); no destruction is drawn; hourglass on 4:7 for the known term."
